### Search telemetry (ENT-1528)

When telemetry is opted in, two additional events measure search ranking
quality for agent-driven search:

- `cli_search_performed` — one event per `entire search` JSON invocation:
  a client-minted `search_id` (ULID, also present in the JSON envelope),
  a `query_hash` (truncated SHA-256 of the normalized query — raw query
  text is never sent), and the served impression set
  (`result_id`, `rank`, `score`, `match_type` per hit).
- `cli_search_result_clicked` — emitted when `entire checkpoint explain <id>`
  resolves an id that appeared in a search served within the last hour:
  `search_id`, `result_id`, `rank`, `seconds_since_impression`, `click_seq`.

Correlation state (the last 20 searches' impression tuples) lives in
`<git-common-dir>/entire/search-impressions.json`, is written only when
telemetry is enabled, and never leaves the machine except as the events
above. Ids are opaque (checkpoint ULIDs / commit SHAs); no prompt content,
file paths, or repo names are included in either event. A best-effort
`session_id` (the agent session's opaque id) is attached when resolvable.
```

